  "id": "psychological-factors",
  "term": "psychological factors",
  "definition": "In this source, psychological factors are the internal and external influences linked with resisting physical activity or stopping participation in real-world exercise situations. They are described mainly as observable emotion-related influences, such as anxiety, depressed mood, and patterns of emotion regulation that contribute to discomfort during or in anticipation of exercise.",
